Subject: Default PHP to the system allocator under Fil-C
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

Zend's allocator hands out request memory from 2 MiB chunks, so Fil-C
bounds a PHP value only by its chunk and reuses freed values' memory
inside it. Use after free and overflows between values then go unnoticed:
the var_destroy use after free in php_var_unserialize() is caught with
USE_ZEND_ALLOC=0 and silently succeeds on Zend's allocator. Make the
tracked system allocator, which PHP's ASan CI uses, the default; it keeps
memory_limit and memory accounting. USE_ZEND_ALLOC=1 restores Zend's
allocator.

tracked_free_all() frees by addresses kept as integers, which have no
capability under Fil-C; leave leftover request memory to the collector.

--- a/Zend/zend_alloc.c
+++ b/Zend/zend_alloc.c
@@ -3026,6 +3026,13 @@
 }
 
 static void tracked_free_all(zend_mm_heap *heap) {
+#ifdef __FILC__
+	/* The keys are addresses, and an integer cast back to a pointer has no
+	 * capability, so free() would trap. Fil-C's collector reclaims the
+	 * request's leftover allocations once nothing refers to them. */
+	(void) heap;
+	return;
+#endif
 	HashTable *tracked_allocs = heap->tracked_allocs;
 	zend_ulong h;
 	ZEND_HASH_FOREACH_NUM_KEY(tracked_allocs, h) {
@@ -3041,8 +3048,20 @@
 
 #if ZEND_MM_CUSTOM
 	tmp = getenv("USE_ZEND_ALLOC");
+#ifdef __FILC__
+	/* Zend's allocator carves request memory out of 2 MiB chunks, so Fil-C
+	 * bounds every PHP value only by its chunk and a freed value's memory is
+	 * reused inside it: use after free and overflows between values go
+	 * undetected. Default to the system allocator, which gives each value
+	 * its own capability, tracked so that memory_limit and
+	 * memory_get_usage() still work. USE_ZEND_ALLOC=1 selects Zend's
+	 * allocator and USE_TRACKED_ALLOC=0 untracked malloc. */
+	if (!tmp || !ZEND_ATOL(tmp)) {
+		bool tracked = !(tmp = getenv("USE_TRACKED_ALLOC")) || ZEND_ATOL(tmp);
+#else
 	if (tmp && !ZEND_ATOL(tmp)) {
 		bool tracked = (tmp = getenv("USE_TRACKED_ALLOC")) && ZEND_ATOL(tmp);
+#endif
 		zend_mm_heap *mm_heap = alloc_globals->mm_heap = malloc(sizeof(zend_mm_heap));
 		memset(mm_heap, 0, sizeof(zend_mm_heap));
 		mm_heap->use_custom_heap = ZEND_MM_CUSTOM_HEAP_STD;
